From: JavaZeroo <2487163254@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Support uint64 zeroing required by native varlen attention

PyTorch varlen_attn creates a uint64 RNG placeholder with torch.zeros.
CANN aclnnInplaceZero rejects DT_UINT64 with error 161002. Zero the same
storage through an int64 view; this preserves the all-zero bit pattern.

This PR1 variant includes only uint64 support. It does not add other
unsigned types or float8 handling from the broader upstream submission.
Backend regression tests are maintained upstream; PR1 uses the Qwen3
training smoke test.

Upstream-PR: https://gitcode.com/Ascend/op-plugin/merge_requests/5801
Upstream-Issue: https://gitcode.com/Ascend/op-plugin/issues/467
Applies-To: 0abe20992cf389c4e9615f96f7198205a155c769

diff --git a/op_plugin/ops/opapi/ZerosLikeKernelNpuOpApi.cpp b/op_plugin/ops/opapi/ZerosLikeKernelNpuOpApi.cpp
index d7967d8..6ecb390 100644
--- a/op_plugin/ops/opapi/ZerosLikeKernelNpuOpApi.cpp
+++ b/op_plugin/ops/opapi/ZerosLikeKernelNpuOpApi.cpp
@@ -22,6 +22,13 @@ using npu_preparation = at_npu::native::OpPreparation;
 
 at::Tensor& zero_(at::Tensor& self) {
   DO_COMPATIBILITY(aclnnInplaceZero, acl_op::zero_(self));
+  // varlen_attn uses a uint64 RNG placeholder; CANN cannot zero this dtype.
+  // An int64 view preserves the storage and the all-zero bit pattern.
+  if (self.scalar_type() == at::kUInt64) {
+    at::Tensor alias = self.view(at::kLong);
+    EXEC_NPU_CMD(aclnnInplaceZero, alias);
+    return self;
+  }
   EXEC_NPU_CMD(aclnnInplaceZero, self);
   return self;
 }
